From: more@chaph.usc.edu (Max More)
Subject: Forum/est - WARNING!

I've known a few people who have taken est ("Erhard Seminars Training" -
the former name for the Forum, changed due to the evil things done by the
founder, Erhard), and I attended an introductory evening around 18 months
ago.

	My impression was negative.  There are probably some useful techniques
in est/The Forum, but they appear to be used largely to psychologically
compel people to work for the higher-ups like slaves, and to spend huge amounts
of money on nemerous courses.  Certainly the people who had just finished the
course were ecstatic and enthusiastic - but then so are Christians for months
are being "saved".  Clever psychological manipulation of persons needing
guidance in life can produce intense emotional experiences.  This is *not*
the same as receiving real, enduring benefit.

	Most Extropians who I know of are strong-minded, and so may be able to
participate in the Forum, drawing what may be useful from it without becoming
slaves to the leaders, but I feel I must sound a warning to counter the two
recommendations.

	Apart from the manner of the main speaker (who was well practiced at
charisma), I found the high-pressure sales tactics of the group leader
disturbing.  Very few people were able to leave without putting down a deposit
for the course.  I also found the group leader to be either ignorant or 
evasive: He cited a study by pollster Yankelovich claiming lasting (self-
reported) benefits from the Forum, but could not tell me where to find these
results, nor who I could ask in the organization who could tell me.

	Again, I have no doubt that the Forum (like Diuretics.. I mean 
Dianetics) contains some valuable self-transformative techniques
(about which I would like to hear more from Extropian participants),
but the organizational use of these and more manipulative techniques 
seems to me to be something to avoid.


